    "done_when": "These writers stop writing JSON through their own temporary-and-rename code and call reckon/_store.py:write_json_atomically with the parameters that keep their current bytes, file mode, fsync, directory fsync and locking:\n- reckon/crew/follow_checkpoint.py: write, append_history and _replace_atomically;\n- reckon/hooks/install.py:_write_settings, which keeps its re-read of the original that refuses a concurrent edit;\n- reckon/project_state.py:_durable_replace, at every call site that stages a JSON payload;\n- reckon/crew/paid_lanes.py:write_document_atomically;\n- reckon/crew/resumption.py:_write_lane_probe_cache;\n- reckon/crew/review.py: _write_record and store_review.\nA call site that stages non-JSON text keeps its current path, as a retained exception with its reason. The writers that fsync the directory today keep doing so through fsync_directory=True.\n\nThe numeric decoders reckon/crew/hold.py:_as_number and reckon/crew/window_reading.py:_numeric call reckon._observations.optional_number, keeping any caller-specific policy in a line around the call. A private helper left with no caller is deleted.\n\nBefore editing, record at base cea6da07, by running the base code:\n- each writer's output bytes and file mode for one fixed payload, under an explicit umask the test sets and restores;\n- whether each writer fsyncs the directory, observed by patching os.fsync;\n- each decoder's output over True, False, 0, 1.5, \"1\", None and a list.\nCommit these as the expectations of tests/test_writer_callers_second_wave.py, which asserts the migrated callers reproduce them. It also asserts that a failure injected mid-write through the shared writer leaves each target holding either its old or its new content.\n\nThat file, tests/test_writer_callers_first_wave.py, tests/test_one_atomic_writer_and_number_decoder.py, and the existing test file of each touched module that has one pass at exit 0. The manifest writes baseline_suite and after_suite each as one line of armed JSON: revision, command with no placeholder, exit_status, completed, failure_count, failure_ids, log_path. The head arm runs at the committed head. Every gate log opens with one line naming its revision, tree and command, and any failing id is listed in failure_attribution as present at base or as caused. The declared negative control is applied and observed to fail, and its log's absolute path is in the manifest with an EXIT= line and the FAILED id. The full project suite is not run by this node.",
    "estimated_hours": null,
